// The float lane's narrow partition of region B: the same interval
// [kX0, kX1) cut until the figure the lane's own recurrence carries
// is under half the lane's budget. Region B has no walk of its own
// to inherit, and the seed's error is amplified by the steps that
// follow it, so a piece is placed by the carried figure and not by
// its fit residual alone: the pieces nearest kX0 come out narrowest.
// One evaluation reads kNarrowBDegF32 + 1 coefficients from the one piece
// the argument falls in, against the shipped seed's kBDeg + 1 from its
// single row.
inline constexpr int kNarrowBDegF32 = 6;
static_assert(
    kNarrowBDegF32 % 2 == 0,
    "a degree the split Clenshaw summation reads must be even: its odd part seeds at c[2m-1] and "
    "assumes the m odd coefficients an even degree has, so an odd degree would drop its leading "
    "odd coefficient and evaluate a different, lower-degree polynomial accurately");
