// The float lane's rational route over its own narrow partition: the
// family's own degree pair per piece, at each piece's own interval and
// mapped argument. The partitions are the narrow Chebyshev ones - a
// partition is a cut of the region, not a property of a family - so a
// piece the family could not hold the target on is bisected, and the
// piece table carries the result. Every row was searched at the narrow
// partition's own aim, half the lane's tolerance, and asked again at the
// lane's own target where an order's binary32 floor stands above the aim;
